-- Q3768: SOC Engagements [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Report it as an operating effectiveness exception in the results section","Ignore the finding if other compensating controls adequately exist","Recommend that management implement the control after report issuance","Report it as a design deficiency since the control was never implemented"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per SSAE No. 18 (AT-C Section 320.35), when a described control was never implemented, this constitutes a design deficiency affecting both the fairness of the system description and the suitability of control design. The auditor must report this finding and evaluate its impact on the overall opinion.
Wrong (A): An operating effectiveness exception applies when a control exists but occasionally fails to function as designed. A never-implemented control is a design-level issue, not an operating failure.
Wrong (B): Compensating controls do not excuse a misrepresentation in the system description. The described control must actually exist for the description to be fairly stated.
Wrong (C): The auditor''s role is to report findings, not to defer them for post-report remediation. A never-implemented control must be addressed in the current engagement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3768;

